### Required staffing (no fixed ratios)
COMAR 10.07.05 sets **no client-to-aide or client-to-RN ratio**. The duties drive the staffing:
- **Registered nurse.** Assesses each new client who needs skilled services or ADL help, helps write the plan of care, decides whether a CNA is needed, and trains aides [S7]. The RN supervises **on site at least every 45 days** if staff administer medications, **every 3 months** if staff assist with self-administration, and **every 4 months** otherwise [S7]. CFC/CPAS also require the agency to *employ* an RN for participant assessments and delegation [S11][S49].
- **Reassessment timing.** Plans of care are reassessed at least annually, on request, and within 48 hours of certain skilled needs or a significant change in condition. When the RN documents that 48 hours is not needed, the deadline becomes 7 days [S7].
- **24/7 on-call.** Clients must be able to reach the agency at any time, with a response within 1 hour, and the agency keeps a log of calls [S7].
- **Governing authority.** It meets at least annually with management and keeps minutes [S47].

### Hiring and screening
Before an aide is referred to a client, the agency must complete [S5]:
- a State criminal history check (or private background check) under Health-General Title 19, Subtitle 19;
- license or certification verification;
- TB and health screening;
- reference and employment-history checks;
- I-9 and identity checks;
- an in-person interview;
- a skills demonstration.

The agency must report possible nursing-practice violations to the Board of Nursing and OHCQ immediately [S5].

### Training
Minimum aide training covers [S6]:
- personal care skills with supervised practice;
- when to call the RN;
- record keeping;
- ethics and confidentiality;
- **CPR**;
- standard infection-control precautions;
- abuse and neglect prevention.

Outside trainers must have OHCQ approval in writing before they train [S6][S1].

### Required systems
- **ISAS (EVV).** Mandatory for CFC/CPAS/CO personal assistance. Up to 5 admin and 5 billing users per agency. Aides cannot log into the portal [S10][S46]. Verify each visit from the participant's primary landline or an OTP device; an aide's phone number should never be the same as the client's [S46].
- **LTSSMaryland provider portal.** Used for reports and service corrections [S46].
- **Private-pay scheduling, EVV and billing software.** Optional, but needed to meet COMAR's itemized-billing and records rules [S48].
- **Medicaid documentation.** Keep records for 6 years and verify eligibility monthly [S59][S49].
- **Annual HCBS Cost Survey.** The FY 2026 survey is due **December 31, 2026**. Non-filers face payment suspension from January 1, 2027 [S12].
- **RSA wage report.** Each RSA files an annual personal care aide wage report with the Department of Labor by September 1 (HB 189 of 2024) [S43].
- **Incident reporting.** Report incidents within 24 hours and submit a written report within 7 days. Report suspected abuse to the local department of social services immediately [S59][S11].

### Employment law costs built into the model
- **Overtime** after 40 hours [S21].
- **Earned sick and safe leave** at 1 hour per 30 worked, paid at 15+ employees [S27].
- **Workers' compensation** (mandatory) [S26].
- **UI tax** of 1.0–2.6% on the first $8,500 of each worker's wages for new employers [S25].
- **FAMLI** at a 0.9% total rate from January 1, 2027. Employers may withhold up to half from employees, and employers with fewer than 15 employees remit only 50% of the rate [S28].
